---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Thermodynamics Cheat Sheet | Free Laws, Engines, Entropy"
  description="Complete thermodynamics cheat sheet with laws, engines, and entropy. Free download for physics and engineering students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Thermodynamics<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Laws, engines, and entropy. From heat transfer to Carnot cycle.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Laws of Thermodynamics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Zeroth Law</h3>
        <pre><code>If A = B and B = C, then A = C
Thermal equilibrium is transitive
Basis for temperature measurement</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>First Law</h3>
        <pre><code>ΔU = Q - W
Internal energy = heat - work
Energy is conserved</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Second Law</h3>
        <pre><code>ΔS ≥ 0 (isolated system)
Entropy always increases
No perfect heat engine (100% efficiency)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Third Law</h3>
        <pre><code>S → 0 as T → 0
Entropy approaches zero at absolute zero
Absolute zero is unattainable</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Heat Transfer</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Conduction</h3>
        <pre><code>Q/t = kAΔT/L
k = thermal conductivity
A = cross-sectional area
L = length</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Specific Heat</h3>
        <pre><code>Q = mcΔT
m = mass
c = specific heat capacity
ΔT = temperature change</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Engines & Refrigerators</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Heat Engine</h3>
        <pre><code>η = W/Q_h = 1 - Q_c/Q_h
η_Carnot = 1 - T_c/T_h
T must be in Kelvin</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Refrigerator</h3>
        <pre><code>COP = Q_c/W = Q_c/(Q_h - Q_c)
COP_Carnot = T_c/(T_h - T_c)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Entropy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Entropy Change</h3>
        <pre><code>ΔS = Q_rev/T
ΔS_total ≥ 0
ΔS = nC ln(T₂/T₁) (constant V)
ΔS = nC ln(T₂/T₁) - nR ln(V₂/V₁) (ideal gas)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
